```text
SUMMARY:
The applicant is requesting a zone change from MU B Mixed-Use Business toPPublic fora 74,168 square
foot site.The site contains a10500square foot office building, agarage, a parking lot and a fleet fueling
stationfor the Cheyenne Housing Authority.The Cheyenne Housing Authority provides decent, safe,
existing use ofthe subject property, a quasi-governmental facility which serves the public of Cheyenne,
is an established and compatible use within neighborhood.Surrounding land uses include alight
commercial utility building, a set of mobile homes, a day care center office, Qwest Communications,
Taco John’s and vacant property.Currently the site resides in and is surrounded by a MUB zone district
which is a district intended for a diverse mix of Residential uses and Non-residential uses which serve
adjacent or nearby neighborhoods.The applicant needs to replace their existing underground fuel tank
with an above ground fuel tank.In order to enable the construction of the above ground fuel tank the
applicant is requesting a zone change toPPublic as an above ground fuel tank is not permitted in the
MUB zone district. Shape Cheyenne, the City's future land use plan, identifies this area as Public and
Quasi-Public. Appropriate uses for the Public and Quasi-Public category are uses related to community
services.The Development Officehas determined that the requested zone changeis supported
substantially for the following reasons.It complies with the future land use plan.It meets the intent of
the proposed P zone district, and lastly the proposed Pzone district is compatible with the surrounding
MUBzone district and existing land uses.
```

